<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Wolfgang von Goethe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1749–1832</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Wolfgang von Goethe was a German poet, novelist, dramatist and scientist, the central figure of German literature. Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>, he won fame with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-sorrows-of-young-werther">The Sorrows of Young Werther</a> in 1774 and from 1775 lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a>, where he served as a minister of Duke Charles Augustus. His works include the drama Faust and the novel Wilhelm Meister's Apprenticeship.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-wolfgang-von-goethe.jpg" alt="Johann Wolfgang von Goethe" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Karl Stieler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goethe_(Stieler_1828).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
